Package: golemirt
Title: Interactive Item Response Theory Models and Estimation
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Dimitrios", "Zacharatos", email = "dzacharatos@yahoo.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Wes", "Bonifay", role = "aut", comment = "author of irtDemo, from which the app is adapted"),
    person("Metin", "Bulus", role = "aut", comment = "author of irtDemo, from which the app is adapted"),
    person("Kostas", "Maistrelis", role = "ctb", comment = "Thurstonian IRT curves")
    )
Maintainer: Dimitrios Zacharatos <dzacharatos@yahoo.com>
Description: A 'shiny' application, built as a 'golem' package, for learning
    item response theory (IRT) with interactive 'plotly' charts. It draws the
    response curves of the Rasch and one- to four-parameter logistic models,
    the partial credit, generalized partial credit, graded response, rating
    scale and nominal response models, the probit response functions of
    Thurstonian IRT, and the response and information surfaces of an item
    that measures two abilities. It also shows how the estimates are found:
    a person's ability by maximum likelihood with the Newton-Raphson method,
    an item's parameters by maximum likelihood on log-likelihood surfaces,
    and a person's ability by expected and maximum a posteriori estimation.
    It brings together the 'modelsirt' and 'mleirt' apps, adapted from the
    'irtDemo' package.
